    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "I'm not sure I follow. If we just focus on 'opportunity' without looking at the outcomes, aren't we just ignoring the fact that historical biases have already skewed the data? If our 'fair' algorithm still results in 90% of loans going to one demographic, haven't we failed our ESG targets? Why is outcome-based optimization seen as a 'distortion' rather than a correction?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
